  "request": {
    "spec": "A person may name other people on the sheet as their patrons, one at a time from their row (not\nthemselves, and not the same person twice; a refusal shows an error on the row; PATRON_ADDED\nname=<name> patron=<patron name>). Show each person's patrons (names, comma and space separated,\nsorted) and their backing: their patrons' due-totals added up, skipping n/a, 0.00 with no\npatrons.\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nA person may name other people on the sheet as their patrons, one at a time from their row (not\nthemselves, and not the same person twice; a refusal shows an error on the row; PATRON_ADDED\nname=<name> patron=<patron name>). Show each person's patrons (names, comma and space separated,\nsorted) and their backing: their patrons' due-totals added up, skipping n/a, 0.00 with no\npatrons.\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
