    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "People can now name other people on the sheet as their patrons, and each row shows their patrons and backing. `bin/e2e` passes: all 4 tests in the spec.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Storage:** a new table, `V18__person_patron.sql`, links a person to each patron by id. Because it stores ids, renaming a patron updates the name everywhere it's shown. The table itself also rejects a person being their own patron or the same patron twice.\n- **Server:** a new endpoint, `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/{personId}/patrons`, takes `{ patronId }`. It refuses, with a 400 and a reason, a missing patron, someone not on the sheet, the person themselves, or a patron already named. A refused request saves nothing and writes nothing to the audit file. A successful one writes `PATRON_ADDED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=<name> patron=<patron name>`. The people list now includes each person's patron names, sorted.\n- **Screen:** each person row has a Patrons cell (`person-patrons`, names joined with \", \"), a picker (`person-patron-select`), an Add button (`person-patron-add`) and an error message (`person-patron-error`). The patron error and the row's other errors clear each other when the next action on the row is taken, as the test rules require.\n- **Backing (`person-backing`):** worked out in the browser, the same way the due-total already is. It adds up the patrons' due-totals, skips n/a, and shows 0.00 when there are no patrons.\n\n**Choices you may want to change**\n- **The picker leaves out the person themselves and anyone already named.** So on screen you usually can't attempt those, and the test's own helper treats a name missing from the list as a refusal. The server still checks both cases and the error appears if one gets through, for example when another user has just added the same patron.\n- **Retired people can still be chosen as patrons.** The request doesn't say, so I didn't exclude them.\n- **Any user can add a patron.** I added no role check.",
